  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1240 AM EDT Sun Sep 27 2026\n\nIn the upper levels, a ridge is over the Great Plains and a closed \nlow is just off the coast of New Jersey. At the surface, high \npressure is over the Great Lakes extending southward to the \nTennessee Valley. A Nor'easter is off the coast of New Jersey \ndrifting westward slowly. Dry, sunny weather with pleasant \ntemperatures will continue today and into Monday with highs mainly \nin the 70s (low 80s near Chattanooga).  \n\nBy Tuesday, the pattern starts to change with a weak ridge over the \nSoutheast and a closed low over the Southwest. At the surface, weak \nhigh pressure is over or just off the coast of the Carolinas. A \nwarming trend will become noticeable by Tuesday with highs in the \n80s for the rest of the workweek (90-91 degrees near Chattanooga). \nDry weather will continue until low rain chances return on Friday. \nHigher rain chances will be possible on Saturday. The slow moving \nsystem to the west will move into the Midwest. A Gulf Low moving \ninto the Southeast along with a ridge centered just east of Florida \nmay bring increasing moisture into the region for next weekend, if \nthat occurs we may see high rain chances next weekend.",
